From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:05:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 180/307] fix: sky light sun-anchored luminance, bounce gain
 normalization, irradiance rolloff

First-round feedback fixes (all three renderers rebuilt):

- Sky light was invisible (0 vs 1000 indistinguishable): the level drives
  its ambient through environment probes, so the TOD GetSkyColor() is
  near black and scaled to nothing. The sky luminance is now anchored to
  the sun (r_LPVSkyLight 1 = 0.2 x sun luminance on an upward facing
  outdoor surface); the TOD sky colour only contributes the hue, with a
  neutral cool fallback when black. The injected lobe is now 60% downward
  cosine + 40% isotropic so it can actually enter interiors through
  vertical openings (windows) - a pure downward lobe barely propagates
  sideways.
- r_LPVSecondaryBounce is now directly the feedback loop gain: the SH
  round trip constant 0.0705 is folded in. Empirical confirmation: the
  user-found equilibrium at raw gain 13 maps to 13 x 0.0705 = 0.92, i.e.
  loop gain ~1. New default 0.5 (old 13 -> new 0.92, old 5 -> new 0.35).
- New r_LPVMaxIrradiance (default 4): Reinhard luminance rolloff on the
  applied irradiance - interiors can be driven with a high intensity
  without overexposing outdoor single-bounce paths and white walls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tu9cj9ax1mqCV93HVfCfpW
